      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nAdds a `docs/deployment/integrations/k8s-aibom.md` page for [k8s-aibom](https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/k8s-aibom), an open-source Kubernetes controller that produces a CycloneDX ML-BOM per serving workload, with vLLM as a natively detected runtime.\n\n## Claims\n\n- One short page in the existing integrations directory, same shape as the KubeAI and KAITO pages; no navigation changes (the directory is globbed).\n- Links to the sibling pages it composes with (KubeAI, KServe, KubeRay, llm-d, production stack) rather than repeating them.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `markdownlint` with `tools/pre_commit/.markdownlint.yaml` passes on the new file.\n- The page appears under Deployment → Integrations in the docs build (globbed directory, alphabetical).\n- The install and plugin commands are the ones in the project's README, in the llm-d guide (`guides/runtime-inventory`), and in the vLLM production stack chart (optional `k8s-aibom` dependency).\n\n## Details\n\nk8s-aibom is already wired into two vLLM-ecosystem projects (production-stack as an optional chart dependency, llm-d as a guide) and into KubeAI as an optional subchart; this page gives vLLM users one place to find it. Detection is read-only toward the cluster and image-pattern based for vLLM (Docker Hub, GHCR, ROCm, ECR, Vertex Model Garden and LMCache image forms), so nothing here depends on vLLM internals.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [ ] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n\n</details>\n",
